::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.W.04] Draft: The author uses good words to make the scene sad. Which revision is most polished? {
~The author uses really good words to make the scene super sad.#Incorrect. This keeps vague and informal language.
=The author uses mournful diction to create a sorrowful mood.#Correct. The revision is precise, academic, and concise.
~The author has words and sadness in the scene.#Incorrect. This is still vague.
~The author writes the scene and it is sad and good.#Incorrect. This lacks precision.
}

::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.L.01] Draft: The evidence supports the claim, it is convincing. Which revision is correct and polished? {
~The evidence supports the claim it is convincing.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
~The evidence, supports the claim, it is convincing.#Incorrect. The commas interrupt the sentence incorrectly.
~The evidence supports, the claim, it is convincing.#Incorrect. This punctuation is incorrect.
=The evidence supports the claim because it is specific and convincing.#Correct. The revision fixes the comma splice and clarifies the relationship.
}

::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.V.03] Draft: The character is mad. Which word is the most precise replacement for "mad" in formal analysis? {
=furious#Correct. "Furious" precisely means very angry.
~nice#Incorrect. This changes the meaning.
~tiny#Incorrect. This describes size, not emotion.
~unclear#Incorrect. This does not mean angry.
}

::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Root clue: The root "scrib" means write. Which word best fits a formal revision about written notes? {
~audible#Incorrect. "Audible" relates to hearing.
~visible#Incorrect. "Visible" relates to seeing.
=transcribed#Correct. "Transcribed" means written or copied down.
~portable#Incorrect. "Portable" relates to carrying.
}

::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.W.04] Draft: This is important because it helps the reader. What is the best publication-polish move? {
~Keep "this" because readers can guess.#Incorrect. Publication-ready writing should not force readers to guess.
=Replace "this" with the specific idea being discussed.#Correct. Naming the idea improves clarity and polish.
~Add more vague words after "important."#Incorrect. More vague wording weakens polish.
~Delete the whole paragraph without checking meaning.#Incorrect. The sentence can be improved through revision.
}
